---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

export const prerender = true;
const UPDATED = '2026-11-07';
const repo = 'https://github.com/MgnCoding2020/burn-and-churn-website';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility statement for the Burn and Churn Coffee portfolio site: the target, how it's tested and known limitations."
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">Accessibility</span>
    <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
    <p class="lede">
      The aim is that everyone can use this site, with a keyboard, a screen reader, a phone or
      high-contrast settings. The target is <strong>WCAG 2.2 level AA</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>How it's tested</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Automated accessibility checks (axe) on every page, at desktop and phone sizes, on every
        change.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keyboard checks: the first Tab reaches "Skip to content"; menus, buttons and drink details
        work by keyboard; focus is always visible and returns where it came from.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every colour pair is checked against the WCAG contrast ratios by a script on every change;
        see the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/design/tokens.md`}>contrast record</a>.
      </li>
      <li>No sideways scrolling at 360 pixels wide.</li>
      <li>
        Reduced motion: if your device asks for less motion, the hero video doesn't play and
        transitions are turned off. Anyone who sees the video can pause it.
      </li>
      <li>Windows high-contrast mode keeps buttons and selected items visible.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>One dark theme.</strong> The site doesn't offer a light version; the{' '}
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/adr/0012-dark-only-public-theme.md`}>decision record</a>{' '}
        explains why. Browser reader modes and high-contrast settings still work.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Unfinished features</strong> such as customer sign-in and ordering are shown as
        unavailable, with text saying so.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Staff sign-out after a time limit.</strong> For security, the staff portal signs
        people out after 1 hour without use. Two minutes before, a dialog says when, and one button
        (or Escape) keeps them signed in. The 8-hour limit on a staff session can't be extended; the
        same warning appears with a link to sign in again. Customers and public pages have no time
        limits.
      </li>
      <li>Testing so far is automated plus the owner's own checks; no external audit yet.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Problems or suggestions</h2>
    <p>
      If something doesn't work for you, please open an issue on{' '}
      <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>GitHub</a> describing the page and what happened. It will be
      treated as a bug.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
